WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.009 --> 00:00:18.790
crossed her fingers so tightly they were going numb as she waited for the robot to call out

2
00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:19.611
the winning number.

3
00:00:19.631 --> 00:00:22.172
"The winning number is 11!"

4
00:00:22.192 --> 00:00:26.514
"Ugh!" Ally collapsed back into her seat.

5
00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:29.815
"There goes my chance of getting back to space."

6
00:00:29.835 --> 00:00:33.221
"I'm so sorry," Mateo said.

7
00:00:34.182 --> 00:00:35.162
She took a deep breath.

8
00:00:35.182 --> 00:00:40.507
"A good Astralian would be happy for the winner."

9
00:00:42.428 --> 00:00:43.829
She looked around the auditorium.

10
00:00:43.849 --> 00:00:48.153
"Where is number 11 anyway?"

11
00:00:49.134 --> 00:00:52.316
The auditorium buzzed as people double-checked their numbers.

12
00:00:53.377 --> 00:00:57.901
When no one claimed the prize, the robot said, "I will select a new number."

13
00:00:57.921 --> 00:01:00.063
"You have another chance!"

14
00:01:00.563 --> 00:01:01.264
Mateo said.

15
00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.548
The robot's lights flashed.

16
00:01:05.929 --> 00:01:09.670
Ally was wishing so hard, she didn't hear the robot call out the new number.

17
00:01:12.811 --> 00:01:15.372
But Mateo jumped up and started cheering.

18
00:01:15.972 --> 00:01:17.112
"You won, Ally!

19
00:01:17.332 --> 00:01:18.273
You won!"

20
00:01:18.653 --> 00:01:22.254
Stunned, Ally ran up to the podium, waving her winning number.

21
00:01:22.274 --> 00:01:25.054
"I'm going back to space!"

22
00:01:25.775 --> 00:01:28.495
As soon as the words came out, Ally covered her mouth.

23
00:01:29.015 --> 00:01:30.516
That's not what she meant to say at all!

24
00:01:31.432 --> 00:01:32.913
The audience burst out laughing.

25
00:01:33.633 --> 00:01:36.915
As Ally looked out at them, she spotted the customer from the diner.

26
00:01:37.655 --> 00:01:41.377
She was sitting in the second row, a mysterious smile on her face.

27
00:01:41.397 --> 00:01:43.138
"It happened again!"

28
00:01:43.519 --> 00:01:43.959
she thought.

29
00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:45.660
"I blurted out the truth.

30
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.281
That woman must be a Carparian!

31
00:01:48.781 --> 00:01:51.043
I'd better stay far, far away from her!"

32
00:01:53.504 --> 00:01:55.685
Ally gave the robot her name and address.

33
00:01:56.225 --> 00:01:58.527
Then the robot handed a printout to Ally.

34
00:01:58.547 --> 00:02:00.888
"These are your instructions.

35
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.201
Follow them exactly or forfeit your prize."

36
00:02:05.662 --> 00:02:08.283
Ally stepped away from the podium, still shocked.

37
00:02:09.984 --> 00:02:11.864
Reporters began flocking around her.

38
00:02:12.385 --> 00:02:13.005
"What's your name?"

39
00:02:13.425 --> 00:02:16.906
"What did you mean when you said you're going back to space?"

40
00:02:17.527 --> 00:02:22.649
The questions were flying faster than an asteroid shower when the robot flashed its lights and made a

41
00:02:22.729 --> 00:02:23.469
new announcement.

42
00:02:23.489 --> 00:02:27.771
"There will be no questions and absolutely no photographs.

43
00:02:28.331 --> 00:02:30.632
If you do not obey this directive, Ms.

44
00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:33.394
Polk will never hold another press conference again."

45
00:02:34.535 --> 00:02:39.719
The reporters reluctantly backed away and made room for Ally and Mateo to exit the museum.

46
00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:45.223
Once they were back outside, Ally read the printout to Mateo.

47
00:02:45.243 --> 00:02:48.485
"'Get ready for the trip of a lifetime!

48
00:02:48.966 --> 00:02:53.789
Lainie Polk will send a car to your residence tomorrow morning to begin training for the flight.

49
00:02:54.129 --> 00:02:54.690
Good luck.'"

50
00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.551
"I can't believe I won!"

51
00:02:56.991 --> 00:02:57.472
Ally said.

52
00:02:58.164 --> 00:03:01.025
"I'm going back to space, and I'll get to meet Lainie Polk.

53
00:03:01.505 --> 00:03:02.846
I wonder what she's like."

54
00:03:03.746 --> 00:03:05.027
Mateo held up his phone.

55
00:03:05.047 --> 00:03:06.648
"I've been reading about her.

56
00:03:07.068 --> 00:03:09.389
She made her first million with an online store.

57
00:03:10.169 --> 00:03:15.631
She's very smart, and her knack for predicting new trends has earned her the nickname the Mind Reader."

58
00:03:16.031 --> 00:03:18.172
His phone beeped as a new text arrived.

59
00:03:18.192 --> 00:03:20.733
"Papi wants us to come to the diner."

60
00:03:20.753 --> 00:03:24.455
"Wait, they call Lainie Polk the Mind Reader?"

61
00:03:24.915 --> 00:03:25.495
Ally asked.

62
00:03:25.515 --> 00:03:29.430
"Mateo, she really might be a Carparian!"

63
00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:30.991
Mateo shrugged.

64
00:03:31.011 --> 00:03:33.993
"Or she might just be a good businesswoman.

65
00:03:34.773 --> 00:03:35.254
Don't worry.

66
00:03:35.774 --> 00:03:37.915
I won't let you be alone with her until we're sure."

67
00:03:37.935 --> 00:03:40.537
"Thanks," Ally said.

68
00:03:40.557 --> 00:03:42.759
"That makes me feel a lot better."

69
00:03:46.941 --> 00:03:50.063
By the time they got back to the diner, it was closed for the day.

70
00:03:51.184 --> 00:03:52.745
Ray and Dawn were in the kitchen.

71
00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:56.648
"We're making a family dinner," Ray announced.

72
00:03:57.068 --> 00:03:58.229
"Can you kids please set a table?"

73
00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:02.753
As Ally and Mateo got to work, Ally watched Ray and Dawn.

74
00:04:03.474 --> 00:04:05.916
"They look so happy," she thought.

75
00:04:05.936 --> 00:04:10.780
"I guess getting them back together is one less thing I have to do before I leave Earth."

76
00:04:14.023 --> 00:04:17.586
After they had finished eating, Ray clinked a spoon against his glass.

77
00:04:18.206 --> 00:04:19.087
"I have an announcement.

78
00:04:20.388 --> 00:04:21.849
I've been thinking about the diner lately.

79
00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:23.451
It's time for a change."

80
00:04:24.331 --> 00:04:24.912
Ally gulped.

81
00:04:26.112 --> 00:04:30.194
Was Ray about to announce he was closing the diner so the family could move to the city?

82
00:04:30.214 --> 00:04:34.356
"I got a call from the bird-watchers' club today," Ray continued.

83
00:04:34.376 --> 00:04:38.277
"The male whooper was spotted flying through the desert with a stick in his beak.

84
00:04:39.158 --> 00:04:41.219
It's proof that the pair is building a nest.

85
00:04:41.779 --> 00:04:46.401
The bird-watchers will be camping out in the desert, searching for the nest, and they asked me to

86
00:04:46.441 --> 00:04:47.982
provide food for all their meals."

87
00:04:48.002 --> 00:04:51.183
"That's great, Papi," Mateo said.

88
00:04:51.203 --> 00:04:53.244
"But what's the change?"

89
00:04:55.136 --> 00:04:56.938
"I bought a food truck to make catering easier.

90
00:04:57.319 --> 00:04:58.920
I'm going to call it Rolling Ray's.

91
00:05:00.402 --> 00:05:05.447
Now we can sell food at all kinds of events—fairs, rodeos, concerts.

92
00:05:06.028 --> 00:05:07.129
The sky's the limit!"

93
00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:10.593
Ray looked so excited, he was beaming like the sun.

94
00:05:11.254 --> 00:05:16.680
But across the table, Dawn crossed her arms, her face darkening like a thundercloud.
